From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: calimocho <calimocho@local>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] winemac.drv: Never block a thread on the app icon set-up

macdrv_SetDesktopWindow runs for every thread's first desktop-window
lookup and used pthread_once for the process-wide app icon. Under
Dredge, the once was entered and never completed, so every later
thread's first window call (XInput's update thread, in RegisterClassExW)
waited forever, and the game's input plugin then hung on quit. The icon
is cosmetic: the first thread still sets it, and no other thread waits.
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/window.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1190,7 +1190,11 @@
  */
 void macdrv_SetDesktopWindow(HWND hwnd)
 {
-    static pthread_once_t app_icon_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+    /* 0: not started, 1: started by some thread. Never wait for the other
+     * thread: the icon is cosmetic, and if its set-up never returns (for
+     * example a user-mode callback left by an exception), a wait here would
+     * hang every later thread's first window call (RegisterClassExW etc.). */
+    static LONG app_icon_started;
     unsigned int width, height;
 
     TRACE("%p\n", hwnd);
@@ -1225,7 +1229,7 @@
         SERVER_END_REQ;
     }
 
-    pthread_once(&app_icon_once, set_app_icon);
+    if (!InterlockedCompareExchange(&app_icon_started, 1, 0)) set_app_icon();
 }
 
 #define WM_WINE_NOTIFY_ACTIVITY WM_USER
